  "foaf:name": "Integrating MSP and Blue Economy in the Caribbean",
  "sdo:name": "Integrating MSP and Blue Economy in the Caribbean",
  "sdo:description": "IMBEC will accelerate climate-smart, nature-positive Blue Economy in the Caribbean SIDS by turning Marine Spatial Planning (MSP) into implementable planning, permitting and investment decisions. Through partnership with Caribbean governments, international and Caribbean non-government organizations, the project will convene a regional MSP+Blue Economy community, deliver a national demonstration (MSP framework, Blue Economy roadmap, and blue transformations for marine industries including fisheries/aquaculture, offshore renewables, tourism and cultural heritage/seascapes), and establish the Caribbean MSP Information Center in Antigua to share data, tools and technical assistance. The initiative will strengthen transboundary cooperation, build local capacity, and enable replication across the Caribbean SIDS through practical guidance and shared learning. It supports Ocean Decade Challenges on ecosystem restoration, a sustainable ocean economy and capacity development.",
